'''Wayland''',<ref name="TFABG" /> also known as '''Weyland''',<ref name="Vader">{{VaderImmortal|I}}</ref> was a [[forest]]ed, [[mountain]]ous [[planet]]<ref name="Kamino Lost audio description">{{TBB|Kamino Lost}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> located in [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]].<ref name="Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> Wayland served as the base of operations of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Imperial cloning program|cloning program]] early in its [[Imperial Era|reign]]. Medical officer [[Doctor]] [[Scalder]] oversaw the [[Tantiss Base|facility]] on the [[planet]]'s [[Mount Tantiss]] and brought in [[Kaminoan]] [[Chief Medical Scientist|Chief Medical scientist]] [[Nala Se]] to work on the Imperial cloning program’s very important [[Project Necromancer]].<ref name="Kamino Lost" /> The research fell under the purview of the [[Advanced Science Division]]<ref name="Tipping Point" /> under [[Chief Scientist]] Doctor [[Royce Hemlock]].<ref name="Metamorphosis">{{TBB|Metamorphosis (episode)}}</ref> The Wayland facility was garrisoned by a number of [[clone commando]]s sporting [[Imperial royal guard|grey markings]] on their armor.<ref name="Kamino Lost" />

Despite the fall of Tantiss Base and the death of Doctor Hemlock in [[Clone Force 99]]'s [[Skirmish on Wayland|Attack on Wayland]], with [[Governor]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] ordering [[Captain]] [[Bragg]] to shutter Tantiss Base indefinitely and redistribute all requested funding and assets for Hemlock’s Imperial cloning program to [[Commander]] [[Orson Callan Krennic]]’s [[Project Stardust]] when they arrived after the Attack,<ref name="The Cavalry Has Arrived" /> the droid [[ZO-E3]] heard that [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]] supposedly had a huge storehouse of treasures on Wayland<ref name="Vader" /> in [[1 BBY]].<ref name="1 BBY Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[Vader Immortal – Episode I]]'' to [[1 BBY]].</ref>

{{Planet-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
===Introduction into canon===
Wayland was first mentioned as a location in ''Star Wars'' [[canon]] in the August [[2015]] [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 32|''Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon'' 32]].<ref name="BTMF">{{BuildFalconCite|32|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> The planet was first shown as a hologram in the [[May 21]], [[2019]] virtual reality video game ''[[Vader Immortal – Episode I]]'',<ref name="Vader" /> and first used as a setting in "[[Kamino Lost]]," the [[August 13]], [[2021]] season one finale of the animated TV show ''[[Star Wars: The Bad Batch]]''.<ref name="Kamino Lost" />

===''Star Wars'' Legends===
In [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]], [[Wayland/Legends|Wayland]] was created by the author [[Timothy Zahn]] and first appeared in the [[1991]] novel ''[[Heir to the Empire]]''.<ref name="Heir to the Empire, 20th anniversary edition">''[[Heir to the Empire: The 20th Anniversary Edition]]''</ref> In the Legends continuity, Wayland's [[Mount Tantiss/Legends|Mount Tantiss]] was home to Emperor [[Palpatine/Legends|Palpatine's]] secret storehouses, including thousands of [[Spaarti cloning cylinder]]s; making the planet used for Imperial cloning technology in both continuities.<ref name="The Last Command">''[[The Last Command]]''</ref>

===Spelling===
The first canon mention in ''Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon'' 32 identifies the planet "Wayland," the spelling used in ''Star Wars'' Legends.<ref name="BTMF" /> This was repeated in [[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]],<ref name="TFABG" /> however ''[[Vader Immortal – Episode I]]'' introduced the spelling "Weyland."<ref name="Vader" /> Later sources have been inconsistent, using both "Wayland"<ref name="Databank" /><ref name="First Order">{{EncyclopediaCite|The First Order}}</ref><ref name="Scarif">{{EncyclopediaCite|Scarif and Other Planets in the Outer Rim}}</ref><ref name="Officers">{{EncyclopediaCite|Imperial Officers and Agents}}</ref><ref name="Five Things">{{SW|url=news/bad-batch-empire|text=5 Things ''Star Wars: The Bad Batch'' Has Revealed About the Rise of the Empire}}</ref><ref name="Metamorphosis EG">{{SW|url=series/the-bad-batch/metamorphosis-episode-guide|text="Metamorphosis" Episode Guide &#124; The Bad Batch}}</ref><ref name="Tipping Point EG">{{SW|url=series/the-bad-batch/tipping-point-episode-guide|text="Tipping Point" Episode Guide &#124; The Bad Batch}}</ref><ref name="Plan 99 EG">{{SW|url=series/the-bad-batch/plan-99-episode-guide|text="Plan 99" Episode Guide &#124; The Bad Batch}}</ref><ref name="Crosshair">{{Databank|crosshair|Crosshair}}</ref><ref name="Mount Tantiss">{{Databank|mount-tantiss|Mount Tantiss}}</ref><ref name="DoR:TVG">''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]''</ref><ref name="Juggernaut Declassified">{{SW|url=news/bad-batch-declassified-juggernaut|text=''Bad Batch'' Declassified: 5 Highlights from "Juggernaut"}}</ref><ref name="Flash Strike EG">{{SW|url=series/the-bad-batch/flash-strike-episode-guide|text="Flash Strike" Episode Guide &#124; Star Wars: The Bad Batch}}</ref><ref name="Flash Strike Declassified">{{SW|url=news/bad-batch-declassified-flash-strike|text=''Bad Batch'' Declassified: 5 Highlights from "Flash Strike"}}</ref><ref name="OSWM">{{GermanFanCite|114|Database}}</ref> and "Weyland"<ref name="Kamino Lost EG" /><ref name="Metamorphosis EG" /><ref name="The Outpost EG">{{SW|url=series/the-bad-batch/the-outpost-episode-guide|text="The Outpost" Episode Guide &#124; The Bad Batch}}</ref> as the spelling.

